# Basic Overlaid Area Chart

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

`fill: "tozeroy"` fills from the trace down to y=0. Multiple traces with `fill: "tozeroy"` overlay.
`mode: "none"` hides the line and shows only the filled area.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: x,
    y: [0, 2, 3, 5, 3],
    fill: "tozeroy",
    mode: "none",
    name: "Trace 1"
  )
)
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: x,
    y: [3, 5, 1, 7, 3],
    fill: "tozeroy",
    mode: "none",
    name: "Trace 2"
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Basic Overlaid Area Chart")
|> Plotly.show()
```
